{{Term/Store|Highland Stable||Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring location in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|'''Highland Stable'''}}|Map|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color TotK|Map Blue|'''Highland Stable'''}}|Map|TotK}}</ref>

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Highland Stable is a [[Stable]] that is located along the [[Faron Highroad]] on [[Fural Plain]], which is part of the [[Faron Grasslands]]. [[Padok]], [[Phanna]], [[Perosa]], and [[Blynne]] are all workers at the Stable. The traveler [[Suzuna]] also resides here. As is the case with all Stables, [[Beedle]] visits as well; Beedle is found sitting outside the entrance to the Stable, but will retreat inside by the main post while it is raining. In {{TCB}} downloadable content pack, the ''[[Super Rumor Mill V3]]'' Book can be found atop the table inside, advancing the "[[EX Ancient Horse Rumors]]" [[Side Quest]].<ref>{{Cite|Apparently {{Color BotW|Red|Highland Stable}} has a copy of Super Rumor Mill EX, which details some rumors about this rare horse gear.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> Phanna can be found tending to [[Horse]]s and is one of the four Stable hands who will offer to customize Link's Horse,<ref>{{Cite|Hello there, traveler. Welcome to our {{Color BotW|Blue|stable}}. You will stay awhile, won't you? If you have a horse, we can help you change its {{Color BotW|Blue|gear}} or {{Color BotW|Blue|mane}} style. We're always happy to meet new horses, so stop on by!|Phanna|BotW}}</ref> provided it has a sufficiently high enough bond and is not too big.

When staying at Highland Stable, Link can choose to [[Sleeping|Sleep]] in either a regular [[Bed]] for 20 [[Rupee]]s or a [[Soft Bed]] for 40 Rupees.<ref>{{Cite|A regular bed will cost you {{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}}. A soft bed is {{Color BotW|Red|40}}.|Padok|BotW}}</ref> Padok explains that the Soft Bed leaves its users feeling more energized when they wake up.<ref>{{Cite|[What's the soft bed?] The soft bed is a special bed we're proud to offer here at the stable. It costs more than a regular bed, but you'll wake up more energized.|Padok|BotW}}</ref> If Link decides to stay at the Stable, Padok offers to wake him up in the morning, at noon, or in the evening.<ref>{{Cite|Sleep until...|Padok|BotW}}</ref> Once Link makes his choice, Padok will send him off to Sleep.<ref>{{Cite|Sleep well!|Padok|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|OK. Rest well!|Padok|BotW}}</ref> When Link wakes up, Padok will greet him.<ref>{{Cite|Good morning. I hope you enjoyed your stay!|Padok|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I hope you enjoyed your stay. Have a good day!|Padok|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I hope you enjoyed your stay. Have a good evening!|Padok|BotW}}</ref> By Sleeping in the Soft Bed, Link will receive an [[Extra Hearts|Extra Heart]] when he wakes up.

Perosa can be found outside tending to the Horses with Phanna, mumbling to herself.<ref>{{Cite|All right, all right!|Perosa|BotW}}</ref> When spoken to, Perosa will complain about the horseback [[Bokoblin]]s that terrorize the northern road.<ref>{{Cite|Is this your first time here?|Perosa|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|[It's my first time.] I see. These plains are home to many quality horses. In the past, nomadic tribes would gather here, but… Nowadays, {{Color BotW|Red|bands of riders}} roam the plains, acting like they own the place.|Perosa|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|I can only hope that someone steps up and deals with those hooligans...|Perosa|BotW}}</ref> If Link offers to help with dispatching the monsters, he will begin the "[[The Horseback Hoodlums]]" Side Quest.<ref>{{Cite|[Leave it to me!] Oh, really? I’m so glad to hear that. I’m counting on you!|Perosa|BotW}}</ref>

Blynne runs the [[Obstacle Course]] [[Mini-Game]] from the Stable. He gives Link a [[Swift Carrot]] for each run he does where he does not beat his record.<ref>{{Cite|Nice riding, fella! You didn't beat my time, but I'm impressed all the same. Here, this is for your hardworking friend.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> If Link completes the course in one minute and thirty seconds, Blynne will give him the [[Extravagant Bridle]].<ref>{{Cite|Here's that {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}} I promised you. Keep at it, and maybe someday you'll be on my level.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref> When Link breaks Blynne’s record of one minute and fifteen seconds, Blynne gives him the [[Extravagant Saddle]].<ref>{{Cite|Holy smoke, would you look at that? Never thought I'd see the day… But a man's gotta abide by his word, so here's that {{Color BotW|Red|horse gear}} I promised.|Blynne|BotW}}</ref>

When "[[Captured Memories]]" is active and Link has already completed "[[Find the Fairy Fountain]]", [[Pikango]] can be encountered at the Stable. While there, he paints a view Fural Plain. He is happy to meet Link again and offers to identify any of his [[Picture]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Hey! We meet again. Are you out traveling as well? I've traveled all over the world, so I'm happy to tell you about new places, if you want. If you have a picture to show me, let's see it already!|Pikango|BotW}}</ref> If Link decides to show him a Picture, he will look at the seventh on in the [[Album]], which depicts the [[Bridge of Hylia]] from a distance.<ref>{{Cite|Hmm... Ah, these {{Color BotW|Red|two tiny stone statues}} depicted here...and that faint view of the {{Color BotW|Blue|Bridge of Hylia}} in the distance...|Pikango|BotW}}</ref> He declares that the Picture was taken along the northeast shore of [[Lake Hylia]], possibly on [[Scout's Hill]] or east of it.<ref>{{Cite|From this angle, I think perhaps this is the northeast shore of {{Color BotW|Blue|Lake Hylia}}. Possibly {{Color BotW|Blue|Scout's Hill}} or perhaps a little further east of there.|Pikango|BotW}}</ref> While that is all he knows, Pikango encourages Link to go out and search for himself.<ref>{{Cite|That's all I know, I'm afraid... Sorry, but you'll have to follow your own feet if you want to find it.|Pikango|BotW}}</ref> On a final note, he believes the statues look like a married couple embracing each other, which he finds charming.<ref>{{Cite|But these statues... They look like a husband and wife embracing. Such a simple yet charming sight.|Pikango|BotW}}</ref>

Link can befriend the [[Hylian Retriever]] behind the Highland Stable. Once it has been fed enough times, it will lead him to a [[Treasure Chest]] buried behind the Stable, which contains a [[Silver Rupee]].<ref>{{Cite Guide|BotW Piggyback|page= 349}}</ref>

